Traversal record for gamma replay (measurement only, bounded-queue path only). Apply after 0001.

SearchParametersHNSW gains trace_d0 / trace_dk / trace_ndis / trace_ids / trace_k. If trace_d0 is
non-null, every base-layer candidate pop appends one row: the frontier d0, d_{k_rule} at that point
(NaN while the auxiliary heap is not yet full), the cumulative base-layer ndis, and the trace_k ids
of the result heap at that point; one final row with d0 = NaN is appended when the loop exits.

The termination rule only decides when to stop, so a search run with gamma equals the gamma = 0
search cut at the first pop where the rule fires. A single gamma = 0 run per query therefore lets
any gamma be replayed offline. The result heap is an abstract handler and cannot be read, so a
shadow heap is maintained with the same faiss heap functions (identical including tie order).
While tracing, the auxiliary d_{k_rule} heap is maintained even at gamma = 0; it is passive, so the
search path is unchanged.

